<title>USA: Propane heating bills seen $100 higher this winter.</title>
<headline>Propane heating bills seen $100 higher this winter.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. residents who heat their homes with propane are to face bills about $100 higher this winter because of the dramatic rise in propane prices, according to analysts and government officials.</p>
<p>Over the past several months, wholesale and retail prices of propane have been driven up by an acute shortage of propane stocks, which are about nine percent below year-ago levels.</p>
<p>While heating oil production and stocks surged in October, efforts in recent weeks to build up propane inventories have been erratic.</p>
</text>
